# Line endings, because one file in this repository is pinned by its hash.
#
# `opensearch/input/synthetic_airports.json` is a committed fixture whose
# SHA-256 is recorded in `opensearch/input/synthetic_airports_source.json` and
# asserted by `opensearch/scripts/verify_airports.py`. A checkout on Windows
# with `core.autocrlf=true` would rewrite every newline and change that hash
# without changing a single data value - the provenance check would then fail
# for a reason that has nothing to do with the data. So: LF everywhere, by
# declaration rather than by hoping the clone is configured correctly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: cmd.exe needs CRLF, and
# `setup_opensearch.bat` / `run_opensearch.bat` are meant to run there.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
